      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i'm looking for. it really feels like the distinction between \"work\" and \"contribution\" is the biggest blind spot for critics. \n\nif we accept that automation is inevitable and the old models are broken, is it even a debate anymore? like, is there any legitimate economic reason to oppose UBI at this point, or is it just political momentum from people clinging to an outdated status quo?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
